# Shell scripts need real LF line endings — a literal CR before the
# newline is a syntax error (bash: "unexpected EOF", confirmed hitting
# this for real while writing infra/scripts/deploy.sh on this Windows
# checkout, where Git's own autocrlf conversion is what introduced the
# CRs in the first place). This forces LF on checkout and commit
# regardless of autocrlf, so it can't recur for this or any later script.
*.sh text eol=lf
